Phase 3 continuation (session 20260926T124402Z)

- Accepted the user's policy decision: Rust source compatibility during the unfinished port is not a requirement; Java RocketMQ 5.5.1 public API and observable behavior remain the acceptance oracle. This batch does not treat remaining parity gaps as waived.
- Audited Java `NettyRemotingClient.getCallbackExecutor()` and `setCallbackExecutor()` against Rust callback dispatch. Java returns the effective executor (callback executor when configured, otherwise public executor; null only when disabled). Rust previously returned `None` by default and ran callback tasks through an internal queue outside its executor trait.
- Implemented a Rust executor adapter for the default client-owned callback queue, routed callback tasks through the selected effective executor, and made `set_callback_executor(None)` restore the default effective executor. Disabled-executor behavior remains getter `None`, ignores assigned executor for dispatch, and runs inline. Changed queue to unbounded to avoid imposing an extra bounded rejection condition on Java executor submission; executor rejection/panic retains the existing inline fallback. Named regression coverage updated in `p3_caller_callback_executor_routes_callbacks_to_owned_executor`.
- Updated `docs/compatibility/PHASE_3_REMOTING_INVENTORY.md`; Java executor ownership/lifecycle and exact queue/thread semantics remain explicitly `PARTIAL`. Phase 3 plan unchanged. Phase 3 is not accepted; Phase 4 not started.
- Validation: `cargo fmt --all --check`; `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --all-features --locked --offline -- -D warnings`; `cargo test --workspace --locked --offline` (all tests passed, including 62 remoting transport integration tests); `python3 scripts/check-workspace-metadata.py`; `python3 tests/differential/compare.py --self-test`; `git diff --check`.
- Code/test commit: `a944224 fix(remoting): expose effective callback executor`. Compatibility inventory update remains to be committed separately.
- Remaining automatable Phase 3 blockers still include executor/worker-group control-flow semantics, pooled buffer reuse, Java config/property loading and encrypted private-key strategy, channel/context API and error/race/lifecycle differences, plus other `PARTIAL`/`NOT MAPPED`/`NOT EQUIVALENT` rows in the inventory. P3-V04 remains Phase 19 only.
